hk: accept a Mach-O LC_UUID as the driver's build id

vkCreateInstance failed with VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED on the M1 ("build-id too short"):
util/build_id.c returns the 16-byte LC_UUID on Apple, Honeykrisp asked for a 20-byte SHA-1.
copy_build_id_to_sha1() zero-pads; the UUID changes with every link, which is what the
pipeline-cache identity needs. SiliconForest's PowerVR build carries the same kind of fix.
Upstream: possible (any Mach-O build of Honeykrisp hits it).

--- a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_instance.c
+++ b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_instance.c
@@ -138,7 +138,13 @@
    }
 
    unsigned build_id_len = build_id_length(note);
+#if DETECT_OS_APPLE
+   /* Mach-O identifies a link by its 16-byte LC_UUID, not a SHA-1 build-id;
+    * copy_build_id_to_sha1() zero-pads it, which is all the cache key needs. */
+   if (build_id_len < 16) {
+#else
    if (build_id_len < BUILD_ID_EXPECTED_HASH_LENGTH) {
+#endif
       result = vk_errorf(NULL, VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED,
                          "build-id too short.  It needs to be a SHA");
       goto fail_init;
